// @trap :18:2
// @hint Intentionally-unused parameter `_n`
// The same unmasked cell one frame DOWN: a message-carrying `__trap__` as the
// only statement of a named function, in a program that prints nowhere.
//
// The import reservation is a whole-program decision (imports occupy wasm
// function indices 0..n-1, so every local function shifts by it), which is why
// `scanPrintUse` walks the entire node arena rather than the top-level
// statements. This file pins that the `__trap__` arm is read off the ARENA and
// not off statement position: on `367ab8d` the module-scope form and this one
// failed identically (no import section, 365 bytes, "type mismatch: expected
// (ref $type), found i32"), and a fix that only looked at top-level statements
// would leave this cell red.
//
// The `assert` shape below is the reason the message form exists at all — it is
// `std:test`'s failure path (std-design D1 OD2).
function assertPositive(_n: i32) {
  __trap__("assertPositive: expected a positive n")
}
assertPositive(-1)
